id:                     E2170
trigger_tool:           configure|clang|cmake|conan
phase:                  configuration|compilation|testing
error_signature:        fatal error: 'guile/gh.h' file not found|fatal error: 'libguile.h' file not found|fatal error: 'gmp.h' file not found
severity:               3
category:               guile|conan-dependency|public-header|transitive-headers|ohos
match_keywords:         libguile.h, guile/gh.h, gmp.h, gc/gc.h, transitive_headers, Guile 2.2, Conan
title:                  Distinguish an omitted published Guile umbrella header from the obsolete gh interface and propagate its public header closure
root_cause:             The published OHOS Guile 2.2.7.1 binary contains libguile/* but omits libguile.h; a consumer's configure then fails modern API detection and falls back to removed guile/gh.h. Supplying libguile.h exposes GMP and GC headers, which Conan does not propagate to downstream consumers by default.
affected_scope:         OHOS Conan consumers of the published guile/2.2.7.1 binary whose public headers include libguile.h or Guile types and whose installed-package consumers compile through Conan-generated targets.
verification_cmd:       Check the exact Guile package include tree for libguile.h and libguile/*; confirm the upstream header version and SHA; inspect configure feature results; run conan create with upstream tests and an installed-package consumer that compiles, links, and executes.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           version-matched-public-header-overlay
rec_description:        Export the exact upstream 2.2.7 libguile.h in the consuming recipe, provide it to configure and the installed package, and mark Guile, GMP, and GC requirements with transitive_headers=True. Keep Guile's published binary unchanged and retain a runtime consumer test.
rec_command:            exports_sources='patches/*'; copy libguile.h from export_sources_folder into source_folder; prepend source_folder to CPPFLAGS for configure; copy libguile.h into package/include; self.requires('guile/2.2.7.1', transitive_headers=True, transitive_libs=True); self.requires('gmp/6.3.0', transitive_headers=True); self.requires('gc/8.2.12', transitive_headers=True)
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe-source-and-requirement-traits
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      repair-and-republish-guile-package
fallback_description:   If the Guile package is under your maintenance scope or its internal headers differ from the verified upstream header, fix that dependency package and rebuild downstream consumers instead of shipping a mismatched overlay.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          manual
forbid_1_pattern:       fabricate.*libguile\.h|copy.*libguile\.h.*different.*version
forbid_1_reason:        An invented or version-mismatched public umbrella header can declare APIs or ABI assumptions absent from the published Guile library.
forbid_1_consequence:   Downstream compilation or runtime can succeed superficially while using incompatible declarations.
forbid_2_pattern:       remove.*Guile|--without-guile
forbid_2_reason:        Guile is libctl's functional API, not an optional runtime detail for this package.
forbid_2_consequence:   A package that skips Guile is not the requested libctl library.
principles:             []
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E158]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/E2170-draft-2501.md
last_updated:           2026-09-25
source_event:           libctl/4.5.1 task 8151 on HarmonyOS PC arm64; missing-header build log SHA-256 77d15854b47684fb6561f3731097ee8a39e4a027366eb20bd822d32674819a55; downstream gmp.h consumer failure SHA-256 f27cbc4f96ab5f7bab26b03a4974a1f1087024f03caded1f36f3b812f464061a; final Conan build and consumer log SHA-256 dc57864d47ea6db069b708bfadf8672e501d0ba8d7ce0659debf792490d27039.
